  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `operation::feed_rating::rated_feed` now takes the document material too. When the material in force on the setup of the op is the document material, the rating is the lower of these two values:\n  - the feed of the tool's cutting-data row for that material;\n  - the running feed of the tool.\n- The post clause (`feed_rating::problems`) and the seed of a new or retargeted Drill or Thread op (`feed_rating::seed_into`, through `cutting_rows::seed_feed_for_tool` and `cutting_rows::retargeted_params`) use the same rating. Thus the check never refuses a feed that the seed sets.\n- A setup whose stock states a different material keeps the rating of its own row. The running feed follows the document material, so it is not a limit for a different material.\n- A running feed that is not a positive, finite number does not lower the rating. The row stays the rating then, as before.\n- `commands/operation/edit.rs` gives the document material to `retargeted_params`.\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2724-hole-feed-running-limit.md` (what was chosen, why, and what was dropped).\n\nNo stored value changes. The post refuses by name. It does not change the feed of the op.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the fix: DR-0600 with a mild-steel row at 115 mm/min, on a mild-steel document, running feed lowered to 80 mm/min. The Drill op at 115 mm/min gave `verify` `ok: true` and posted (the pin failed at `hole_feed_rating.rs:275`, `left: Bool(true)`).\n- After the fix: `verify` is `ok: false`, and `post` refuses with `D: feeds 115 mm/min, above the 80 mm/min that tool DR-0600 states - ...`. A new Drill op on the tool seeds 80 / 80. With the op at 80 mm/min, the program posts, and each drill cycle line has `F80`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `hole_feed_rating::a_running_feed_lowered_below_the_material_row_is_the_rating` (new). It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- `hole_feed_rating::a_running_feed_raised_above_the_material_row_keeps_the_row_rating` (new, review fix). The running feed is 200 and the steel row is 115. The op at 200 is refused at the post with `D: feeds 200 mm/min, above the 115 mm/min`, and a new Drill op seeds 115 / 115. With `max` in `rated_feed`, this test fails (mutation run, source put back). The running feed alone also gives 200, so this test fails for that rule too.\n- `hole_feed_rating::a_stock_material_other_than_the_document_is_rated_by_its_own_row` (new, review fix). The document is mild steel, the stock is brass (row 150), and the running feed is 80. The op at 150 passes `verify`, a new Drill op seeds 150 / 150, and an op at 160 is refused against 150. When the running feed applies for each material, this test fails (mutation run, source put back).\n- `hole_feed_rating::a_row_feed_that_is_not_usable_gives_the_running_feed` (new, review note 2). A row feed of 0, NaN, infinity or -5 gives the running feed (90) as the rating.\n- The other `hole_feed_rating` tests and `tool_cutting_rows` pass with no change.\n\nGate on head b60839ed0 (the review fix, merged with `origin/main` at 20c81cbc1):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test hole_feed_rating --test tool_cutting_rows --test cutting_unknown_row --test lathe_workholding_kinds --locked`: 7 + 11 + 9 + 10 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored (`lathe_workholding_kinds`, as on main).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib --locked`: 287 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nEarlier quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on head 174da2b81: 22 steps, 0 failed.\n\nThis pin also covers the row \"Drill with a material-specific cutting-data row\" of the checklist in #2725 (row E). The other rows of #2725 are not in this PR. Refs #2725\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A Thread op with a named row and a lowered running feed (same function as the Drill path; the pin uses the Drill).\n- Inch projects, tap cycles and the GUI.\n- Example goldens: no `examples/*.nc` or `.camproj` changed. The seed changes only when a tool's running feed is below its row for the document material.\n\nChangelog: A Drill or Thread operation that feeds above its tool's running feed is now refused at the post also when the tool has a cutting-data row for the material at a higher feed; a new Drill or Thread operation takes the lower of the two feeds. A project saved before this change can be refused at its next post when a tool's running feed is below its row; the stored feeds do not change.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2724\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
